seg-f26f0e79f2ed = The real-data holdouts (a and c) are public, because anyone can download the data. They guard against choosing a split after seeing scores, not against tuning on those folders. The sealed holdout of task (d) is a commit and reveal: the owner commits only the hash to <c1/> and keeps the seed (none is sealed yet).

# text
# c1: kshana jammertest score
seg-81c3f961230b = Task (a) truth is the scheduled attack slots of the event logs at one-minute resolution, so a detection probability is a lower bound; the event-level metrics (latency, missed alarms, false alarms) arrive with the Jammertest scorer of <c1/>.

